{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.voltcore.liquid
  ───────────────────────────────────────
  One-product landing page for the Voltcore 2-Piece Set. In the admin:
  Pages → Voltcore → Template suffix → "voltcore". Renders inside
  layout/theme.liquid, which supplies <main>.

  Styles live in site/theme/pages.css and theme-hivolt.css. build-theme.py
  concatenates both into assets/hivolt.css, which the layout already links.

  Everything on this page is read from the live product. Price, sizes, stock
  state, fabric weight and composition all come from Shopify — so the page
  cannot drift out of step with the product it sells, and a price change in
  admin updates the saving arithmetic here automatically.

  The saving is COMPUTED, not typed. The product description used to claim
  "$10.98 less than buying them separately" when the components were $38 and
  $54 against a $79 set — a real saving of $13.00. That is what happens when a
  number is written by hand once and the prices move underneath it. Here the
  component products are looked up by handle and the arithmetic is done in
  Liquid, so it is right or it does not render at all.

  Four things are deliberately absent, because none of them would be true:

    · There is no "cut from one fabric" line. The bra is 75/25 nylon-spandex
      and the leggings are 80/20 — three different blends were being described
      as one. What IS shared, and verified on all three products, is the
      220 g/m² weight, so that is the claim the page is built on.
    · There are no reviews, ratings or testimonials. The store has zero orders,
      so every one of them would be fabricated.
    · There is no urgency furniture of any kind — no timer, no stock warning,
      no viewer count. All three would be inventions.
    · There is no "unworn" condition on returns. The 60-Day Love-It Guarantee
      explicitly covers worn and washed items, and the product copy had been
      contradicting it in the customer-unfriendly direction.

  check-liquid.py enforces most of that list.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign set = all_products['voltcore-2-piece-set-twist-front-bra-flare-leggings'] -%}
{%- assign bra = all_products['women-s-twist-front-v-neck-sports-bra'] -%}
{%- assign legs = all_products['women-s-high-waisted-flare-leggings'] -%}

{%- if set == blank or set.id == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%} The product was renamed, archived or unpublished. Say so
  plainly rather than rendering a landing page for nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="pg pg--solo wrap">
    <div class="rte">
      <h1 class="sec__h">Not available</h1>
      <p>This set isn't currently published.
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Browse everything else</a> —
        every style lists its fibre composition and fabric weight.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- else -%}

{%- assign v = set.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
{%- assign parts_total = 0 -%}
{%- if bra.price > 0 -%}{%- assign parts_total = parts_total | plus: bra.price -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if legs.price > 0 -%}{%- assign parts_total = parts_total | plus: legs.price -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign saving = parts_total | minus: set.price -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'Voltcore Set' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

{%- comment -%} ── Hero: the number is the thesis ───────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">Drop 04 — Voltcore</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">Both pieces.<br>Same knit.<br><em>220 g/m².</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    Most matching sets pair a light top with a heavier bottom, and the mismatch
    shows the moment you move. These are knit at the same weight, so they hang,
    stretch and hold their shape together.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="pg__cols">

    <div>
      {%- if set.featured_image -%}
        <img src="{{ set.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
             alt="{{ set.featured_image.alt | default: set.title | escape }}"
             width="{{ set.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ set.featured_image.height }}"
             style="width:100%;height:auto">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">
      <h2 class="sec__h">{{ set.title | escape }}</h2>

      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Price</span>
          <span class="sheet__v"><em>{{ set.price | money }}</em></span>
        </div>
        {%- if saving > 0 -%}
          <div class="sheet__row">
            <span class="sheet__k">Bought separately</span>
            <span class="sheet__v">{{ parts_total | money }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="sheet__row">
            <span class="sheet__k">You save</span>
            <span class="sheet__v"><em>{{ saving | money }}</em></span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if set.metafields.spec.gsm != blank -%}
          <div class="sheet__row">
            <span class="sheet__k">Fabric weight</span>
            <span class="sheet__v"><em>{{ set.metafields.spec.gsm }} g/m²</em></span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if set.metafields.spec.composition != blank -%}
          <div class="sheet__row">
            <span class="sheet__k">Composition</span>
            <span class="sheet__v">{{ set.metafields.spec.composition }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="sheet__row">
          <span class="sheet__k">Shipping</span>
          <span class="sheet__v">Free, US</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sheet__src">
        Every figure above is read from the product record, not typed onto this
        page. Change a price in admin and the saving recalculates itself.
      </p>

      {%- form 'product', set, id: 'voltcore-buy', class: 'opt' -%}
        {%- unless set.has_only_default_variant -%}
          <div class="opt__lab">
            <label class="mono" for="voltcore-size">Size</label>
            {%- assign sg = pages['size-guide'] -%}
            {%- if sg != blank and sg.handle != blank -%}
              <a href="{{ sg.url }}">Size guide</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endunless -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The select IS the control. An earlier version rendered radio buttons
          named opt-1 beside a hidden select and wired nothing between them —
          so choosing L submitted whatever variant happened to be selected by
          default. A picker that silently adds the wrong size is worse than a
          plain select, and this page ships no JavaScript to bridge them.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <select name="id" id="voltcore-size" class="cf__in" style="max-width:220px">
          {%- for variant in set.variants -%}
            <option value="{{ variant.id }}"
                    {% if variant == v %}selected{% endif %}
                    {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
              {{ variant.title }}{% unless variant.available %} — sold out{% endunless %}
            </option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>

        <button class="btn add" type="submit" name="add"
                {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
          {%- if v.available -%}Add the set — {{ set.price | money }}{%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
        </button>
      {%- endform -%}

      <p class="cf__note">
        Free US shipping. 60-day returns, and you can have trained in it.
      </p>
    </aside>

  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ── Why 220 ──────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="pub">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head">
      <h2 class="sec__h">Why the weight is the whole argument</h2>
      <span class="mono">Published, not claimed</span>
    </div>

    <div class="pub__grid">
      <div class="pub__c">
        <p class="pub__n">180–200</p>
        <h3 class="pub__t">Where most leggings sit</h3>
        <p class="pub__d">
          Light enough to feel good on the hanger. Light enough to go sheer at
          the bottom of a squat, which is where you find out.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pub__c">
        <p class="pub__n">220</p>
        <h3 class="pub__t">Where these sit</h3>
        <p class="pub__d">
          Dense enough to stay opaque through full range and hold shape rep
          after rep. It is a fabric property, not a claim about the fabric.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pub__c">
        <p class="pub__n">Both</p>
        <h3 class="pub__t">Bra and leggings alike</h3>
        <p class="pub__d">
          The pieces use slightly different blends because a support piece and
          a compression piece are engineered differently. The weight is what
          we match, and weight is what governs opacity and drape.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ── What's in it, priced from the live products ──── {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="cat wrap">
  <div class="sec__head">
    <h2 class="sec__h">The two pieces</h2>
    {%- if saving > 0 -%}
      <span class="mono">{{ parts_total | money }} apart · {{ set.price | money }} together</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    {%- if bra.id != blank -%}
      <a class="item" href="{{ bra.url }}">
        <div class="item__fig">
          {%- if bra.metafields.spec.gsm != blank -%}
            <span class="item__gsm">{{ bra.metafields.spec.gsm }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if bra.featured_image -%}
            <img src="{{ bra.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                 alt="{{ bra.featured_image.alt | default: bra.title | escape }}"
                 width="{{ bra.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ bra.featured_image.height }}"
                 loading="lazy">
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="ph"><span>No image</span></div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="item__body">
          <h3 class="item__name">{{ bra.title }}</h3>
          <p class="item__meta">{{ bra.metafields.spec.composition | default: bra.type }}</p>
          <div class="item__foot">
            <span class="item__price">{{ bra.price | money }} on its own</span>
            <span class="item__buy">View</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if legs.id != blank -%}
      <a class="item" href="{{ legs.url }}">
        <div class="item__fig">
          {%- if legs.metafields.spec.gsm != blank -%}
            <span class="item__gsm">{{ legs.metafields.spec.gsm }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if legs.featured_image -%}
            <img src="{{ legs.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                 alt="{{ legs.featured_image.alt | default: legs.title | escape }}"
                 width="{{ legs.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ legs.featured_image.height }}"
                 loading="lazy">
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="ph"><span>No image</span></div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="item__body">
          <h3 class="item__name">{{ legs.title }}</h3>
          <p class="item__meta">{{ legs.metafields.spec.composition | default: legs.type }}</p>
          <div class="item__foot">
            <span class="item__price">{{ legs.price | money }} on its own</span>
            <span class="item__buy">View</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ── Objections, answered straight ────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="faq__h">The questions worth asking</h2>
    <div class="faq__list">

      <details>
        <summary>Is it actually squat-proof, or is that just a word?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">
          It is a consequence of the knit density. At 220 g/m² there is enough
          yarn per square metre that the fabric does not thin out when stretched
          across the widest part of a deep squat. That is why we publish the
          number instead of the adjective — you can compare 220 against anything
          else you own.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why do the two pieces have different fibre blends?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">
          Because a support piece and a compression piece are engineered
          differently. The bra is 75% nylon / 25% spandex; the leggings are
          80% nylon / 20% spandex. What is matched is the weight — both at
          220 g/m² — and weight is what governs opacity and how the fabric
          drapes. We would rather tell you they differ than average the two
          numbers into one that describes neither.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What if the fit is wrong?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">
          Both pieces run true to size. Between sizes, size up for the bra and
          stay true for the leggings. If it is still wrong, you have 60 days —
          including after you have trained and washed it — and returns inside
          the US are free with a prepaid label.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Are there reviews?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">
          No. This is a new store and nobody has left one yet. We would rather
          say that than print testimonials nobody wrote — which is exactly what
          the specification on this page is for. Judge the fabric weight, then
          judge the garment for 60 days at our risk.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How long does delivery take?</summary>
        <p class="faq__a">
          Free standard shipping within the United States, 2–4 business days to
          dispatch and 8–14 business days to arrive. We ship within the US only.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">{{ set.price | money }}{% if saving > 0 %} · {{ saving | money }} less than the pieces{% endif %}</span>
      Sizes S–XL, matte black. Free US shipping, and 60 days to decide after
      you have actually trained in it.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="{{ set.url }}">Go to the product page</a>
  </div>
</section>

{%- endif -%}
